1
00:00:01,559 --> 00:00:05,559
moment, evidently in order to drink a toast.

2
00:00:05,559 --> 00:00:11,719
A large jug was circulating, and the mugs were being refilled with beer.

3
00:00:11,719 --> 00:00:18,280
No one noticed the wondering faces of the animals that gazed in at the window.

4
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:23,159
Mr. Pilkington of Foxwood had stood up, his mug in his hand.

5
00:00:23,159 --> 00:00:28,520
In a moment, he said, he would ask the present company to drink a toast.

6
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:34,319
But before doing so, there were a few words that he felt it incumbent upon him to say.

7
00:00:34,319 --> 00:00:40,159
It was a source of great satisfaction to him, he said, and he was sure to all

8
00:00:40,159 --> 00:00:46,639
others present, to feel that a long period of mistrust and misunderstanding

9
00:00:46,639 --> 00:00:50,360
had now come to an end.

10
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:57,040
There had been a time, not that he or any of the present company had shared such sentiments,

11
00:00:57,040 --> 00:01:03,319
but there had been a time when the respected proprietors of Animal Farm had been regarded,

12
00:01:03,319 --> 00:01:08,680
he would not say with hostility, but perhaps with a certain measure of

13
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:12,360
misgiving by their human neighbors.

14
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:15,200
Unfortunate incidents had occurred.

15
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,280
Mistaken ideas had been current.

16
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:26,639
It had been felt that the existence of a farm owned and operated by pigs was somehow abnormal,

17
00:01:26,639 --> 00:01:31,239
and was liable to have an unsettling effect in the neighborhood.

18
00:01:31,239 --> 00:01:39,000
Too many farmers had assumed, without due inquiry, that on such a farm a spirit of license

19
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,200
and indiscipline would prevail.

20
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:46,520
They had been nervous about the effects upon their own animals

21
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:49,959
or even upon their human employees.

22
00:01:49,959 --> 00:01:54,120
But all such doubts were now dispelled.

23
00:01:54,120 --> 00:02:00,559
Today, he and his friends had visited Animal Farm and inspected every inch of

24
00:02:00,559 --> 00:02:03,079
it with their own eyes.

25
00:02:03,079 --> 00:02:05,280
And what did they find?

26
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:11,440
Not only the most up-to-date methods, but a discipline and an orderliness

27
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:16,159
which should be an example to all farmers everywhere.

28
00:02:16,159 --> 00:02:21,239
He believed that he was right in saying that the lower animals on Animal Farm

29
00:02:21,239 --> 00:02:27,840
did more work and received less food than any animals in the county.

30
00:02:27,840 --> 00:02:33,319
Indeed, he and his fellow visitors today had observed many features which they

31
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:37,840
intended to introduce on their own farms immediately.

32
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:42,520
He would end his remarks, he said, by emphasizing once again the friendly

33
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:50,040
feelings that subsisted and ought to subsist between Animal Farm and its neighbors.

34
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:55,879
Between pigs and human beings, there was not and there need not be

35
00:02:55,879 --> 00:02:59,120
any clash of interests whatever.

36
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:02,760
Their struggles and their difficulties were one.

37
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:06,840
Was not the labor problem the same everywhere?

38
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:08,959
Here, it became apparent that Mr.

39
00:03:08,959 --> 00:03:14,319
Pilkington was about to spring some carefully prepared witticism on the company.

40
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:20,600
But for a moment, he was too overcome by amusement to be able to utter it.

41
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:28,079
After much choking, during which his various chins turned purple, he managed to get it out.

42
00:03:28,079 --> 00:03:33,479
>> If you have your lower animals to contend with, we have our lower classes.

43
00:03:33,479 --> 00:03:37,120
>> This bon mot set the table in a roar.

44
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:40,879
And Mr. Pilkington once again congratulated the pigs on the low

45
00:03:40,879 --> 00:03:46,760
rations, the long working hours, and the general absence of pampering, which he

46
00:03:46,760 --> 00:03:49,680
had observed on Animal Farm.

47
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:55,079
"And now," he said finally, he would ask the company to rise to their feet

48
00:03:55,079 --> 00:03:58,920
and make certain that their glasses were full.

49
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:02,879
>> "Gentlemen," >> concluded Mr. Pilkington.

50
00:04:02,879 --> 00:04:09,280
>> "Gentlemen, I give you a toast to the prosperity of Animal Farm."

51
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:12,799
>> There was enthusiastic cheering and stamping of feet.

52
00:04:12,799 --> 00:04:17,799
Napoleon was so gratified that he left his place and came round the table to

53
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:23,360
clink his mug against Mr. Pilkington's before emptying it.

54
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:26,000
When the cheering had died down, Napoleon, who had remained on his feet,
